## What I did

The task file's deliverables 1–3 were largely landed by Day 207 (the general sweep audit_table_against_models_dev, the comparator, and the network test already exist). I checked rather than assumed: unaudited_shipped_rows and the doc comment both returned zero hits, so those two pieces were genuinely missing. I built exactly those.

1. The census for the direction the comparator is structurally blind to. ours_from_catalogue builds yoyo's side from the catalogue, so every row reaching compare_catalogue is by construction one the source carried — a table row models.dev never mentions never enters the comparison at all, and an omission that reports nothing looks exactly like a clean bill. unaudited_shipped_rows enumerates the population from the repo's own side and names the ids the source omits, printing the count with the sample and asserting examined > 0. Its bound is stated in the doc: the ids providers::known_models_for_provider ships for PROVIDER_KEYS — so the contains-matched arms no provider table lists sit outside it and are reported by the Day-204 alarm, never silently counted as audited here.

2. The doc comment above `builtin_model_pricing` naming both ignored commands. I resolved the exact test names rather than guessing, and noted that price_drift_audit is a prefix of price_drift_audit_against_models_dev.

3. Three offline tests. A two-direction census test (omitted id named; carried id not; examined independent of the source), an anti-vacuous test asserting an empty source makes every examined id unaudited, and deliverable 3(d) as a behaviour test: eight (estimated)-commented arms driven through the ordinary comparator with a 3× perturbation on the table's own reading — so a skip set would show up as compared == 0, and the assertion stays true whichever number is eventually verified.

Positive control, one atomic mutate→run→restore: neutering the census's ids.push reddened exactly the two census tests by name while the eight-arm test stayed green; restore verified by grep (0 occurrences of the marker). Register pasted 3439 → 3455.

One thing I got wrong twice and want on the record: I first wrote the register prose from my plan ("seven-line doc comment", "1037 lines") instead of my diff. Both were wrong — 9 lines, 1142 lines — and I fixed both from measurement. That is the Day-202 defect recurring in the exact file whose purpose is tracking reality.

